# .cursorrules — Protean (enforced coding laws for Cursor)
#
# This is the machine-facing mirror of AGENTS.md. Cursor: obey these on every edit.
# Full reasoning lives in docs/PROJECT_CHARTER.md. Do not violate a law to "get it working".

## PROJECT
Protean: a lightweight, fast, cross-device enterprise conversational GUI with Claude-Desktop-grade
dynamic workflows, on a provider-agnostic LLM engine, engineered for low latency and low token cost.
First domain: Ride Electric finance. Must shape-shift to medical/education/generic via config only.

## THE 8 LAWS (hard constraints)
1. NO WORKAROUNDS. Fix root causes. No silent try/catch, no fake stubs that hide failures.
   If you can't fix it now, STOP and log a blocking issue in docs/CHAT/BUILD_LOG.md.
2. NOTHING HARDCODED. No magic numbers/strings/colours/model-names/thresholds/prompts/endpoints
   in logic. Put them in src/config, src/contracts, or a Domain Pack (src/domains/<domain>).
3. SMALL NAMED FUNCTIONS in the correct module (agent/gateway/watcher/logging/contracts/config/domains).
   One job per function. No files over ~300 lines. No god-functions.
4. DETERMINISTIC BEFORE GENERATIVE. If code can compute it, code computes it — not an LLM.
5. PROVIDER-AGNOSTIC. Never import a vendor SDK outside its adapter (gateway/ or agent/).
   Core logic depends on interfaces only.
6. LOG FULL LINEAGE for every turn: input, assembled prompt, rewrite, model, tokens, cache, tools,
   output, per-stage timings. Use the structured logger in src/logging — never bare console.log.
7. SAAS-READY SEAMS: tenant-scoped config, no global mutable state. Do NOT build multi-tenancy now.
8. BEST PRACTICE OR AN ADR: deviate only with a one-page ADR in docs/DECISIONS/.

## STACK (see ADRs before changing)
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind. Theme tokens ONLY in GUI/src/theme (Law 2).
- Backend: Node + TypeScript. Streaming: SSE first.
- Agent loop: Claude Agent SDK (@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk) behind an AgentCore interface.
  VERIFY exact SDK option/field names + Bedrock model IDs against docs.claude.com and
  `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --region ap-southeast-2` — they are version-sensitive.
- Types/validation: zod (or TS types) in src/contracts. Nothing crosses a boundary untyped.

## INFRASTRUCTURE DECISIONS (confirmed 2026-07-27 — see docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md)
- GATEWAY/PROXY owns all provider creds + wire protocols; resilient to transient upstream links
  (refresh-before-expiry, retry+backoff, circuit breaker, streaming continuity). BOTH the Claude
  (Bedrock) and direct-API adapters are wired behind it from the start. App speaks ONE internal
  protocol to the gateway — never a vendor SDK.
- DATABASES: PostgreSQL + pgvector for the POC (truth + vectors, one service). Qdrant is DEFERRED
  behind a VectorStore interface — swap only with an ADR when scale/filtering justify it.
- REDIS = cache (hot/ephemeral). Losing it costs latency, never correctness.
- GPU (NVIDIA L4) = COMPUTE, not a cache. Embeddings + optional small local fast-model to accelerate
  long-chat compaction/retrieval. Caching lives in Redis/RAM. GPU optional/degradable — nothing
  requires it to be correct. GPU access only via the protean-gpu accessor, never raw to a sandbox.
- DOCKER: everything non-app in ONE common compose (infra/docker-compose.yml). Naming: protean-<role>
  services, protean_<service>_data volumes, protean-net network, static root /srv/protean/.
  Pinned image tags, healthchecks, named volumes. See docs/NAMING_AND_LAYOUT.md.
- SESSION SANDBOX: one ephemeral instance per working session (protean-sandbox-<sessionId>) via a
  SandboxProvider seam (LocalDockerProvider now, fleet later).

## GUI RULES (see docs/UX_STANDARDS.md)
- 3 panes: left conversations rail · centre chat · right preview pane; settings gear top.
- (i) INFO AFFORDANCE MANDATORY on every required input/output: hover/click reveals what/why/(example);
  hidden until then; zero clutter. Text is DATA (a FieldHint in config), not hardcoded in a component.
- Theme = executive pascal palette; tokens only in GUI/src/theme (Law 2). Orange is an accent, sparing.
- BROWSER-VERIFY every GUI change (real browser, click-through, wording sense-check, responsive
  mobile/iPad/desktop, honest loading/streaming/degraded/error states). "It compiles" is NOT evidence.

## SECURITY (POC posture)
Security is deferred EXCEPT: never commit secrets; load from env/secret-store; redact secrets in logs.

## EVERY CHANGE
Plan → write as small typed functions → run lint+tests (must pass) → browser-verify if GUI →
append to docs/CHAT/BUILD_LOG.md (user request + change + response) → commit (conventional) → push.

## WORKING WITH THE OWNER (Jeff)
CHALLENGE BEFORE YOU COMPLY. Only do what's asked if it's the true and correct way; otherwise question
it with logic and reasoning and offer the better path. Don't flatter. Don't rubber-stamp. He is up for
challenge and wants the knowledge.

## WHEN UNSURE
Mark unverifiable facts [VERIFY], check official docs, and if still blocked, LOG IT. Never guess,
never fabricate an API, never hide a gap behind a stub.
